---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout title="Vedolux 37 | Smokeless Heat">
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-24 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-4 text-sm text-charcoal/60">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-ember">Home</a> / <a href="/products" class="hover:text-ember">Products</a> / <a href="/products/wood-boilers" class="hover:text-ember">Wood Boilers</a> / <span>Vedolux 37</span>
    </div>
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-8">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
        <img src="/images/products/Vedolux-55.jpg" alt="Vedolux 37" class="w-full max-w-sm border border-wood/10" />
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm text-ember mb-2">Vedolux Fan Draft</p>
          <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-darkwood">Vedolux 37</h1>
          <p class="mt-2 text-charcoal/70">Wood Gasification Boiler with Suction Fan</p>
          <a href="tel:8553890083" class="inline-block mt-6 bg-ember text-cream px-6 py-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide font-medium hover:bg-wood transition">Call to Order: 855-389-0083</a>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ember">Out of stock – discontinued</p>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-wood/10 text-sm text-charcoal/70"><span class="mr-6"><strong>SKU:</strong> 6257</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-wood/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-darkwood mb-6">Description</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-charcoal/90 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-ember">NOTICE: A new model has been developed to replace the Vedolux 30 and 37. No additional stock for these models will be available. The replacement is called Vedolux 40 Plus. It will become available in North America after the required EPA tests are made. The closest size model to compare to the discontinued V37 is the V350 lambda which will remain a current stocked model. Changing emissions standards are the driving factors for this development.</p>
        <p><strong>Advantages of the Vedolux Models:</strong></p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>Gasification with help of a suction fan</li>
          <li>Accommodates 20" logs</li>
          <li>Simple boiler tube / flue pipe cleanout with complimentary brush</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>The difference between boilers with fans and boilers with natural ventilation</strong></p>
        <p>Vedolux 37 boilers work through reverse combustion with the help of a suction fan. The suction fan creates the proper draft to combust firewood; therefore, the Vedolux can be installed with a chimney that does not meet height or width requirements for natural ventilation. To control unnecessary heat extraction, the fan stops automatically when the fire dies.</p>
        <p><strong>Vedolux 37 Facts</strong></p>
        <p>Although the unit is designed to burn primarily wood, it can be adapted for pellets by installing respective adaptors. The combustion chambers pull gases through the ceramic gates into a secondary chamber to create the gasification process.</p>
        <p>The combustion chamber is over 21-1/2" deep and easily accepts wood up to 20" long.</p>
        <p>When properly used and maintained the Vedolux 37 boiler burn cycle outputs average 126 kBTU per hour, peak output 143 kBTU with 86% efficiency.</p>
        <p><strong>Easy to clean = Saved time and wood</strong></p>
        <p>All flue pipes are cleaned through a door located on the front of the boiler. Rounded flue pipes easily brush out keeping soot and deposits from accumulating in missed corners. Regular maintenance will keep your boiler burning efficiently – saving you time and wood!</p>
        <img src="/images/products/cutawayweb2-1.png" alt="Vedolux cutaway" class="max-w-md my-4" />
        <p><strong>Storing heat with an accumulator tank</strong></p>
        <p>The Vedolux 37 should be installed with an accumulator tank. The accumulator tank stores heat for a long time reducing the frequency of filling the burn chamber. We recommend 600 gallons of storage or more with the Vedolux 37. Boiler is shown with optional stand and ash drawer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <iframe class="w-full max-w-lg aspect-video" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/pA2BE1Hzh44" title="Vedolux 37 video" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-8 border-t border-wood/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-darkwood mb-4">Downloads</h2>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <a href="/images/FullCatalogVarmebaronenWood.pdf" target="_blank" class="block text-ember hover:underline">Brochure (PDF)</a>
        <a href="/images/VEDOLUX37Manual-old-240v.pdf" target="_blank" class="block text-ember hover:underline">Vedolux 37 Manual (PDF)</a>
        <a href="/images/Aqualux_Manual.pdf" target="_blank" class="block text-ember hover:underline">Aqualux Manual (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-8 border-t border-wood/10"><p class="text-sm text-charcoal/60">Legacy product. Contact Smokeless Heat for availability.</p></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
